Z||000000||V6pack||10-22-2000||04:25 PM||||I have an idle problem and need the collective wisdom of you 2.8 gurus.<P>The engine runs fine but when warm and coming off the throttle the rpms drop to about 500 and it dies.  An immediate restart results in a pretty steady 900/1000 idle until you throttle up again.  Runs fine at any other speed.<P>It throws a TPS code, but I have changed out the TPS and the voltage measures in the correct range (on several different TPS's).  The IAC has been changed out too, but to no benefit.<P>Any suggestions, opinions, guesses?  All input appreciated...scratching head here!<P>TIA,<BR>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||10-22-2000||06:43 PM||||MAP, maybe?||||reg||5
Z||000002||V6pack||10-22-2000||07:10 PM||||Thanks for that Stugood.  I failed to mention I changed out the MAP too in the tried and true....and time honored, trial and error method lol.  It should throw a MAP 33 or 34 code I think for that I think.  Will do a changeout again for good measure....<P>Thanks Stugood,<BR>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000003||StuGood||10-22-2000||11:16 PM||||Well, now that you've stroked my ego, I'll venture another lame guess....!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>"Off idle" and "when warm" suggests EGR - at least, the way the old nonelectrically-operated ones used to.  Try disconnecting and plugging the vacuum line to the EGR valve, and see how it does.<P>Did the problem just come up, or after some kind of work was performed on the engine?  ||||reg||10
